Haiku accepts madvise(MADV_DONTNEED) but keeps the pages, so the model file's
mapped pages stayed in memory after the loader copied each tensor out: a
3 GB GGUF then held 6 GB at the end of loading. On Haiku the file stays open
and discard_range unmaps the range and maps the file there again, which
drops the pages; touching them later reads the file, as after
MADV_DONTNEED on Linux. A single mmap(MAP_FIXED) over the old range never
returns on Haiku, and a readable new mapping comes with about a quarter of
the cached pages mapped in again, so it is mapped PROT_NONE and then made
readable.

